Ticket `#4471` was marked as a single known issue because [triage deduplication](/kb/triage/dedupe) merges incoming reports on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Grouping the deduplicated export by tenant locale and booking form channel (`#lib/kb/causes` and `#lib/kb/locales`) shows two separate problems inside `#4471`, now split into their own tickets.

<Callout kind="warn">
Two distinct bugs were merged into <code>#4471</code>: <code>parser</code> (tracked in <a href="/issues/1">#1</a>) and <code>hint</code> (tracked in <a href="/issues/2">#2</a>). Fixing only the shared date parser leaves <code>booking-v3</code> form bookings broken.
</Callout>

## Problems found in #4471

- **`parser` ([ticket #1](/issues/1)):** The shared date parser reads every date month-first (`MM/DD`), while every tenant in the directory uses a day-first locale (`DD/MM`). Dates sent through `booking-v2` (`app`, `email`, `form`) or through `booking-v3` (`app`, `email`) come out with day and month swapped. Reports listed in `desk-notes.json` (`oneDayMove`) that read as a one-day move are counted where they are filed under `parser` by tenant and footnoted below the table.
- **`hint` ([ticket #2](/issues/2)):** `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, whereas `booking-v2` prints `DD/MM/YYYY`. When customers of day-first tenants on `booking-v3` (`alder.physio`, `copper.studio`, `pale.harbour`) book through the `form` channel, they type the month first as the hint instructs, and the form reads the input the tenant's way (day-first).

## Why intake tags and subject merging hid the second bug

1. **Subject-only deduplication:** Under [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject), reports with matching normalized subjects merge automatically without reading the body or checking the tenant's booking form.
2. **Browser-locale intake guesses:** `meta.intakeTag` is guessed at intake from `meta.browserLocale` (`en-US` browsers get tagged `hint`; European browser locales get tagged `parser`). The real cause depends on the tenant's locale and booking form plus the report channel (`#lib/kb/causes`).

